From 9d0b1b059fb6327976184ca14c4c7b2a06fbb67c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:29:31 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/60] Graph cache: a capture is freed until the map holds it,
 the keep floor stays under the max, a max of 0 is eager

- A capture whose agreement throws, or whose insert runs out of memory, no longer leaks its executable: the map's
  slot is reserved before the capture, and the executable is owned here until the insert, which cannot fail.
- A host map that cannot grow counts as no room in the existing room vote, so every rank declines that miss together.
- `min_keep` is clamped to `max`, so under the memory floor the cap never rises above the configured max. A max of 0
  runs every step eagerly, with no collective.
- A cap lowered to 0 under the floor goes back to max once every rank has room, instead of staying eager for good.
- Hits make no collective: with `Agree` set, keys, settings and fingerprint changes must already match on every rank.
  The docs now say so: the fingerprint changes at the same step on every rank, and `fingerprintOf` is for one rank.

Co-authored-by: Jonathan Regan-Beasley <197533392+jregan-beasley-smc@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from commit 3cc0397482e01bbf88f3dcfbbded98725e0eeca1)
---
